{
  "slug": "artist:lil-peep",
  "name": "Lil Peep",
  "editorial_article": "Born Gustav Elijah Åhr in Allentown, Pennsylvania, Lil Peep moved to Long Beach, New York, as a toddler before eventually settling in Los Angeles in 2016 to pursue a music career. His debut studio album, Come Over When You're Sober, Pt. 1, was released on August 15, 2017, via First Access Entertainment and AWAL. Known as a pioneer of the emo rap genre, he combined trap production with influences from punk bands such as The Cure and Blink-182. His breakthrough mixtapes, Crybaby and Hellboy, featured DIY production he often mastered himself. He died on November 15, 2017, in Tucson, Arizona, from an accidental overdose of fentanyl and alprazolam. Following his death, his estate oversaw posthumous releases including the 2018 album Come Over When You're Sober, Pt. 2, which peaked at number four on the Billboard 200.",
